{title: 171 - Thine Is the Glory}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #171 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 171}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Thine is the glory, [Bb]Risen, [Bb7]con[Eb]quering [Bb]Son;
[Eb]Endless is the victory [Fm]Thou [Eb]o'er [Bbsus]death [Bb7]hast [Eb]won.
[Eb]Angels in bright [Bdim7]rai [Cm]ment [Bdim7]Rolled [Cm]the [Bdim7]stone [Cm]a[G]way,
[Cm]Kept the folded [F7]grave-clothes [Gm]Where [Cm]Thy [F]bod[F7]y[Bb]lay.
[Eb]Thine is the glory, [Bb]Risen, [Bb7]con[Eb]quering [Bb]Son;
[Eb]Endless is the victory [Fm]Thou [Eb]o'er [Bbsus]death [Bb7]hast [Eb]won.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Eb]Thine [Bb]is [Bb7]the glory, [Eb]Risen, [Bb]conquering Son;
[Eb]Endless [Fm]is the [Eb]victory [Bbsus]thou o'er [Bb7]death [Eb]hast won.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Lo! [Bb]Jesus meets [Bb7]us. [Eb]Risen from [Bb]the tomb,
[Eb]Lovingly [Fm]He [Eb]greets us, [Bbsus]Scatters [Bb7]fear [Eb]and gloom;
[Eb]Let [Bdim7]His [Cm]Church [Bdim7]with [Cm]gladness [Bdim7]hymns [Cm]of [G]triumph sing,
[Cm]For [F7]her [Gm]Lord now [Cm]liveth; [F]Death has [F7]lost [Bb]its sting.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]No [Bb]more we [Bb7]doubt Thee, [Eb]Glorious Prince [Bb]of life!
[Eb]Life [Fm]is nought [Eb]without Thee; [Bbsus]Aid [Bb7]us in [Eb]our strife;
[Eb]Make [Bdim7]us [Cm]more [Bdim7]than [Cm]conquerors [Bdim7]through [Cm]Thy [G]deathless love
[Cm]Bring [F7]us [Gm]safe [Cm]through Jordan [F]to [F7]Thy [Bb]home above.
{end_of_verse}
